Định dạng JUnit để tuần 26–30/10 nối vào GitHub Actions.

### 16:00–16:30 · Viết `docs/testing-strategy.md` cho hoàn chỉnh

```markdown
# Testing strategy

## The shape
Most of the value sits in fast unit tests over pure functions. Component tests
cover the parts with real interaction — mainly forms. End-to-end tests are
deliberately few: three flows that would make the app useless if they broke.

| Layer | Tool | Count | Runtime |
|---|---|---|---|
| Unit — pure logic | Jest | ~40 | < 5s |
| Component | Jest + RNTL | ~15 | ~15s |
| Network layer | MSW | included above | — |
| End-to-end | Maestro | 3 flows | ~2 min |

## What I don't test, and why
- Third-party libraries — they have their own suites
- Implementation details — refactors would go red without a real bug
- Styling and colours — brittle, catches nothing
- Full-screen snapshots — everyone updates them without reading the diff

## Why Maestro over Detox
Maestro needs one CLI install and no changes to the app. Detox needs native
build configuration and a separate test target — one to three days of setup.
For a project this size, Maestro gives the same confidence for far less
maintenance. Detox is the better call when you need deep synchronisation with
native module timing, which this app doesn't have.
```

