## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Năm: Câu hỏi phỏng vấn

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

### 16:40–16:55 · Trả lời có ghi âm

**Câu hỏi tuần này:** *"How do you handle authentication and token refresh in a mobile app?"*

> *"Tokens go in SecureStore — the Keychain on iOS, the Keystore on Android — never in AsyncStorage, because that's just an unencrypted file in the app sandbox.*
> *Access tokens are short-lived, so the interesting part is what happens when one expires. If five requests are in flight and they all get a 401, and each one fires its own refresh call, most backends rotate the refresh token — so the first refresh succeeds and the other four are now using a revoked token. The user gets signed out even though they did nothing wrong.*
> *So I gate it. The first 401 starts a refresh and stores the promise. Any other request that hits a 401 while that's in flight awaits the same promise instead of starting its own. When it resolves, all of them retry with the new token. If the refresh itself fails, I clear the session and send the user to the login screen — and I also clear the query cache so no data leaks to the next account.*
> *I built exactly this in my current project and verified it by dropping the JWT lifetime to sixty seconds and leaving the app idle."*

**Câu cuối là câu mạnh nhất.** Nó chuyển bạn từ *"tôi biết lý thuyết"* sang *"tôi đã làm và đã kiểm chứng"*.

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `in flight` | đang trên đường (request) | *Five requests are in flight.* |
| `gate` (v) | chặn / kiểm soát lối vào | *So I gate the refresh.* |
| `rotate` (v) | xoay vòng, cấp mới thu cũ | *The backend rotates refresh tokens.* |
| `revoked` (adj) | đã bị thu hồi | *They're using a revoked token.* |
| `leak` (v) | rò rỉ | *So no data leaks to the next account.* |

